'''Jiban Jyoti Panda''' is an Indian scientist specializing in the field of nano-biotechnology. She received the  [[L'Oréal-UNESCO Awards for Women in Science|UNESCO - L`Oreal For Women in Science Fellowship]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.unesco.org/new/en/natural-sciences/priority-areas/gender-and-science/for-women-in-science-programme/2011-fellowships/|title=2011 Fellowships &#124; United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization|access-date=2016-11-10|archive-date=2016-08-22|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160822073657/http://www.unesco.org/new/en/natural-sciences/priority-areas/gender-and-science/for-women-in-science-programme/2011-fellowships/|url-status=live}}</ref>
<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.unesco.org/new/fileadmin/MULTIMEDIA/HQ/SC/pdf/sc-pdf_scholarships_FWIS_2001_EN.pdf |title=UNESCO-L'OREAL International Fellowships in Life Sciences - 2011 |date=3 November 2010 |publisher=[[UNESCO]] |access-date=2016-11-10 |archive-date=2016-11-10 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161110235036/http://www.unesco.org/new/fileadmin/MULTIMEDIA/HQ/SC/pdf/sc-pdf_scholarships_FWIS_2001_EN.pdf |url-status=dead}}</ref>

== Education ==
Panda started her education by enrolling at [[Utkal University]] in the state of [[Odisha]] in India.{{cn|date=June 2026}} She completed her Bachelor of Science (Honours) in chemistry, zoology and botany in 2003. She subsequently completed her [[Master of Science]] degree in the field of biotechnology from the same university in 2005. Later, she went on to complete a Ph.D. in biotechnology at the [[International Centre for Genetic Engineering and Biotechnology]], India, in 2012.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.inst.ac.in/faculty/dr_jyoti.html|title=Institute of Nano Science and Technology|access-date=2016-11-10|archive-date=2016-11-10|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161110173039/http://www.inst.ac.in/faculty/dr_jyoti.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Research==
Her primary interests are in the field of Nano-biotechnology. She works on the design and synthesis of novel bio-compatible and multi-functional nano-structures for achieving targeted and effective drug delivery to different organs especially the organs like brain and eye, which are protected by different physiological barriers and are inaccessible to drugs administered via the oral and [[parenteral]] routes.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.businesstoday.in/magazine/features/brain-tumour-treatment-nanotech-based-drug-delivery-system/story/15469.html|title=Treating brain tumour with a nanotech-based drug delivery system|date=26 May 2011|access-date=10 November 2016|archive-date=10 November 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161110235147/http://www.businesstoday.in/magazine/features/brain-tumour-treatment-nanotech-based-drug-delivery-system/story/15469.html|url-status=live}}</ref> She also designs bio-compatible drug delivery systems for effective cancer therapy.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.modyuniversity.ac.in/cash/pdf/LECTURE_WORKSHOP.pdf |title='Science Academies' Lecture Workshop on "Emerging Technologies based on Nanoscience- A popularization workshop" |date=22–23 April 2016 |website=[[Mody University]] |access-date=10 November 2016 |archive-date=25 November 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161125231315/http://www.modyuniversity.ac.in/cash/pdf/LECTURE_WORKSHOP.pdf |url-status=live }}</ref>
<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://meta.science/author/111163188_jiban_jyoti_panda |title=Archived copy |access-date=2016-11-10 |archive-date=2016-11-10 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161110174440/https://meta.science/author/111163188_jiban_jyoti_panda |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal |doi = 10.2217/nnm.12.201|title = Modified dipeptide-based nanoparticles: Vehicles for targeted tumor drug delivery|journal = Nanomedicine|volume = 8|issue = 12|pages = 1927–1942|year = 2013|last1 = Panda|first1 = Jiban J.|last2 = Kaul|first2 = Ankur|last3 = Kumar|first3 = Santosh|last4 = Alam|first4 = Shadab|last5 = Mishra|first5 = Anil K.|last6 = Kundu|first6 = Gopal C.|last7 = Chauhan|first7 = Virander S.|pmid = 23398497}}</ref>

Developing novel methods for effective blood brain barrier delivery for treating [[glioblastomas]] and other neurodegenerative disorders as well as developing and characterizing different drug nano-formulations with enhanced activity are also her main focus of research. She has published numerous papers in peer reviewed journals.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Jiban-Panda |title=Profile: Jiban Panda |website=[[ResearchGate]] |access-date=2022-06-03 |archive-date=2022-06-03 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220603135537/https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Jiban-Panda |url-status=live }}</ref>

